{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_016zpq3Hv8XcxpX1cTW9tMWi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# \n2\t<p width=\"100%\" style=\"align:center\">\n3\t<img height=\"150\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rdentato/skp/master/docs/oval_logo_small.png\"> <br/>\n4\t \n5\t</p>\n6\t\n7\tSkp is a library of functions to help parsing text files.\n8\t\n9\tIt offers three *levels*:\n10\t  - **Skipping**, where the focus is to identify portion of text that can be skipped according a pattern;\n11\t  - **Scanning**, where a text is repeatedly checked against a set of patterns;\n12\t  - **Parsing**, where a Parsing Expression Grammar can be directly coded as a recursive descent parser.\n13\t\n14\tSkp assumes that the text is UTF-8 encoded, ISO-8859-1 encoding can also be used.\n15\tBeing the focus on parsing programming languages and data files, the character classes\n16\t(uppercase/lower, digit, ...) are limited to the ASCII range.\n17\tOther clasess can be specified explicitly. For example you can match an hiragana character\n18\twith `[ぁ-ゖ]`.\n19\t\n20\tFor further information have a look at the [documentation](https://rdentato.github.io/skp/) or chat with us on <a href=\"https://discord.gg/vPgsxHcgXX\"><img src=\"https://github.com/rdentato/skp/blob/master/docs/Discord_button.jpg?raw=true\" title=\"Discord Channel\"></a>. \n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c920d18c-1f9c-4e1a-b9e1-9a1b9d710a9b","uuid":"9cf96d59-3abc-45ca-b47b-eac3a3dec4c4","timestamp":"2026-05-28T22:16:25.792Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/harvest-crust-xtM7Eh/project/c_src/README.md","content":"# \n<p width=\"100%\" style=\"align:center\">\n<img height=\"150\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rdentato/skp/master/docs/oval_logo_small.png\"> <br/>\n \n</p>\n\nSkp is a library of functions to help parsing text files.\n\nIt offers three *levels*:\n  - **Skipping**, where the focus is to identify portion of text that can be skipped according a pattern;\n  - **Scanning**, where a text is repeatedly checked against a set of patterns;\n  - **Parsing**, where a Parsing Expression Grammar can be directly coded as a recursive descent parser.\n\nSkp assumes that the text is UTF-8 encoded, ISO-8859-1 encoding can also be used.\nBeing the focus on parsing programming languages and data files, the character classes\n(uppercase/lower, digit, ...) are limited to the ASCII range.\nOther clasess can be specified explicitly. For example you can match an hiragana character\nwith `[ぁ-ゖ]`.\n\nFor further information have a look at the [documentation](https://rdentato.github.io/skp/) or chat with us on <a href=\"https://discord.gg/vPgsxHcgXX\"><img src=\"https://github.com/rdentato/skp/blob/master/docs/Discord_button.jpg?raw=true\" title=\"Discord Channel\"></a>. \n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
